The '''Incisor Sidestep''' was a [[hyperspace route]] that connected [[Anoat]]<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" />&mdash;a [[planet]] in the [[Anoat sector]]<ref name="Uprising">''[[Star Wars: Uprising]]''</ref>&mdash;and [[Sullust]]<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" />&mdash;a [[planet]] in the [[Brema sector|Sullust sector]]<ref name="Tarkin" />&mdash;both in the [[Outer Rim Territories]] region of [[the galaxy]]. As such the route acted as a connection between the much longer [[Corellian Trade Spine]] and [[Rimma Trade Route]], as Anoat and Sullust also sat on those routes respectively.<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" />

Sullust also acted as a junction from the Incisor Sidestep onto the secret [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Sanctuary Pipeline]] to the [[moon]] of [[Endor]].<ref name="Moving Target" /> The former [[pirate]] [[Queen]] [[Maz Kanata]] marked the Incisor Sidestep as one of the "real" routes for [[smuggler]]s to use, as oppose to the official ones, on a map that she included in the [[book]] that would eventually become known as the ''[[Smuggler's Guide]]''.<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Incisor Sidestep was first mentioned in the [[2018]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: Smuggler's Guide]]'', which was written by [[Daniel Wallace]].<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" />

